 61ZN cQ $Q(|ep)=835 {I16}, S(2n)=25276 {I16}, S(2p)=9771 {I16} (2012Wa38)      
 61ZN c  {+61}Zn produced and identified by 1955Li39 in the bombardment of      
 61ZN2c  {+58}Ni by 15-22 MeV |a particles followed by chemical separation.     
 61ZN3c  An earlier abstract by Cumming (Phys. Rev. 99, 1645|a (1955)) and      
 61ZN4c  a later full paper 1959Cu86 confirmed this isotope                     
 61ZN c  Theory, calculations:                                                  
 61ZN d  1976Da02: calculated mass excess.                                      
 61ZN c  2002Ca48: large-scale shell model calculations.                        
 61ZN d  2003Mi23: relativistic mean field (RMF) theory, calculated binding     
 61ZN2d  energy and quadrupole deformation                                      
 61ZN c  2004Ho08: the effective interaction GXPF1 for shell model              
 61ZN2c  in the pf shell.                                                       
 61ZN cG E,RI$Primarily From {+28}Si({+36}Ar,2pn|g) (2009An01) and/or           
 61ZN2cG {+40}Ca({+24}Mg,2pn|g) (2006An31), where in-beam |g-ray data are       
 61ZN3cG most comprehensive. For low-lying levels (below 2.5 MeV),              
 61ZN4cG energy and intensity data from (|a,n|g) (1984Th07,1982Sm01) are        
 61ZN5cG also considered in the averaging procedure. Exceptions are noted       
 61ZN cG M$From |g|g(|q) and |g(lin pol) data in high-spin studies              
 61ZN cG E(X)$Doublet structure                                                 
 61ZN cL $Note that in 1999-Nuclear Data Sheets (1999Bh04), 88.2, 418.3, and    
 61ZN2cL 756.0 levels were erroneously assigned half-lives of <430 ms, 0.14 s   
 61ZN3cL {I7} and <130 ms, respectively. These half-lives in 1999Oi01 simply    
 61ZN4cL refer to the half-life of the decaying {+61}Ga isotope                 
 61ZN cL E$Level energies with |DE<8 keV are deduced from least-squares fit     
 61ZN2cL to the Adopted Gammas (by evaluators). The others are weighted         
 61ZN3cL averages of all available data from ({+16}O,{+13}C),({+6}Li,t) and     
 61ZN4cL ({+3}He,{+6}He).                                                       
 61ZN cL J$For states with J|>9/2, assignments are essentially as proposed in   
 61ZN2cL the high-spin studies by 2009An01 and 2006An31, which are based on     
 61ZN3cL |g|g(|q) and |g(lin pol) data for selected transitions, band           
 61ZN4cL assignments, decay pattern of levels, and yrast nature of population   
 61ZN5cL of levels in heavy-ion |g-ray studies, except as noted. The            
 61ZN6cL parentheses in many cases have been added by the evaluators            
 61ZN cL $For band configurations in terms of quasiparticle notation,           
